{
  "node_type": "statement",
  "body": {
    "id": "prop:tangent-fan-global-cover",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "Suppose \\(p_0\\in\\operatorname{relint}(\\mathcal P_{\\mathrm{ASC}})\\) and \\(\\operatorname{im}(B)\\subseteq\\operatorname{lin}(\\mathcal P_{\\mathrm{ASC}}-p_0)\\).  Then every \\(u\\in\\mathbb R^d\\) has a compatible lift \\(p_0+tBu\\in\\mathcal P_{\\mathrm{ASC}}\\) for all sufficiently small positive \\(t\\), admits a feasible optimal symbolic completion in \\(\\mathcal B_0\\), and belongs to at least one completed semantic cell.  Hence\n\\[\n \\bigcup_{v\\in V}D_v^0=\\mathbb R^d.\n\\]\nEquality signs belong to all incident completions.  More generally, use the causally compatible offset space\n\\[\n \\mathcal K_0=\\{A_\\Psi z:z\\in\\operatorname{lin}(\\mathcal P_{\\mathrm{ASC}}-p_0)\\}.\n\\]\nIf \\(c_n\\to c\\in\\mathcal K_0\\), the compact-uniform moving remainders vanish, and a compact \\(C\\) has distance at least \\(\\tau>0\\) from every hyperplane \\(c_j+a_j'u=0\\), then the lawful multinomial label on \\(C\\) eventually equals the label generated by \\(D_v^0(c)\\).  At \\(c=0\\) this is the label fan of \\(\\mathfrak G_0\\).  If there are no active cuts, there is one retained global semantic label and the honest diameter minimax value is zero.",
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:causal-base-relative-interior",
      "ass:tangent-image-compatible",
      "ass:local-family-affine-hull",
      "ass:multinomial-base-convergence",
      "ass:multinomial-local-expansion",
      "def:compatible-observed-law-polytope",
      "def:label-fan",
      "def:moving-slack-system",
      "def:multinomial-label-regions",
      "lem:compatible-observed-law-polytope",
      "lem:relative-interior-tangent-lift",
      "lem:compatible-lift-completed-cover",
      "lem:compact-causal-domain",
      "lem:compact-moving-remainder-covariance",
      "prop:fiber-polytope-equivalence"
    ],
    "justification": "The corrected proposition derives legal symbolic completions from the compatible observed-law polytope and a proved relative-interior lift.",
    "gap": "Its proof can be attached after the new domain assumptions and structured definitions are adjudicated; no ambient-simplex neighborhood is used.",
    "consumer": "It validates the global cover condition for the zero-offset Gaussian experiment and the causal moving-offset space.",
    "proof_tex": "Put \\(L=\\operatorname{lin}(\\mathcal P_{\\mathrm{ASC}}-p_0)\\).  By\n\\(\\text{ass:causal-base-relative-interior}\\),\n\\(\\text{ass:tangent-image-compatible}\\), and\n\\(\\text{lem:relative-interior-tangent-lift}\\), for every\n\\(u\\in\\mathbb R^d\\) there is \\(t_u>0\\) such that\n\\[\n p_0+tBu\\in\\mathcal P_{\\mathrm{ASC}}\n \\qquad(0<t\\leq t_u).\n\\tag{1}\n\\]\nBy \\(\\text{lem:compatible-observed-law-polytope}\\) and\n\\(\\text{prop:fiber-polytope-equivalence}\\), every law in (1) has a\nnonempty finite response-type fiber, so all of the finitely many branch\noperations and endpoint programs in \\(\\mathscr L_0\\) admit feasible\noptimal symbolic completions.\n\nChoose a sequence \\(t_k\\downarrow0\\).  Since the set of symbolic branch\nand primal--dual optimal completions is finite, a subsequence has one\nconstant completion \\(b\\).  If\n\\(\\psi(p)=\\alpha_\\psi'p+\\beta_\\psi\\in\\mathscr L_0\\) and\n\\(\\psi(p_0)\\ne0\\), continuity implies that the sign along this\nsubsequence is its frozen base sign.  If \\(\\psi(p_0)=0\\), affinity gives\nthe exact identity\n\\[\n \\psi(p_0+t_kBu)=t_k\\alpha_\\psi'Bu.\n\\tag{2}\n\\]\nConsequently the constant completion chooses the weak tangent sign\nprescribed by \\(\\alpha_\\psi'Bu\\).  If\n\\(\\alpha_\\psi'Bu=0\\), both weak inequalities hold, which is precisely\nthe stipulated incidence convention.  Passing the finite weak linear\ninequalities and the finite primal--dual feasibility and optimality\nequalities to the limit shows that \\(b\\in\\mathcal B_0\\) is a feasible\noptimal completion at \\(u\\).  Thus \\(u\\in P_{v,b}^0\\) for the semantic\nprojection \\(v\\) of \\(b\\).  This is also the conclusion of\n\\(\\text{lem:compatible-lift-completed-cover}\\), and hence\n\\[\n \\bigcup_{v\\in V}D_v^0=\\mathbb R^d.\n\\tag{3}\n\\]\nIdentity (2) proves directly that a zero tangent slack belongs to every\nincident weak completion.\n\nWe next prove the moving-offset assertion.  Let \\(A_\\Psi\\) be the\nmatrix with rows \\(\\alpha_j'\\) for\n\\(j\\in\\mathcal J_0^{\\mathrm{act}}\\).  Since every active cut satisfies\n\\(\\psi_j(p_0)=0\\), the definition of \\(c_n\\) gives\n\\[\n c_n=\\sqrt n\\,A_\\Psi\\{p_n(0)-p_0\\}.\n\\tag{4}\n\\]\nBy \\(\\text{ass:local-family-affine-hull}\\), the vector in braces lies\nin \\(L\\).  Therefore (4) proves\n\\(c_n\\in A_\\Psi L=\\mathcal K_0\\); offset compatibility is derived rather\nthan assumed.\n\nSuppose now that \\(c_n\\to c\\in\\mathcal K_0\\), that the moving\nremainders converge uniformly on compact sets as stated, and that a\ncompact set \\(C\\) has positive distance from every hyperplane\n\\(c_j+a_j'u=0\\).  When the active index set is nonempty, compactness,\nfiniteness, and the nonzero normal condition give\n\\[\n \\delta_C\n :=\\min_{u\\in C}\\min_{j\\in\\mathcal J_0^{\\mathrm{act}}}\n       |c_j+a_j'u|>0.\n\\tag{5}\n\\]\nWhen the active set is empty, the following sign argument is vacuous.\nConvergence of \\(c_n\\) and compact-uniform convergence of the\nremainders imply that, eventually,\n\\[\n \\max_j|c_{n,j}-c_j|\n +\\max_j\\sup_{u\\in C}|e_{n,j}(u)|\n <\\frac{\\delta_C}{2}.\n\\tag{6}\n\\]\nUsing the defining identity\n\\[\n \\zeta_{n,j}(u)=c_{n,j}+a_j'u+e_{n,j}(u),\n\\tag{7}\n\\]\nthe reverse triangle inequality and (5)--(6) show that\n\\(\\zeta_{n,j}(u)\\) and \\(c_j+a_j'u\\) have the same strict sign,\nsimultaneously for every \\(u\\in C\\) and every active \\(j\\).\n\nFor completeness, if \\(\\psi(p_0)\\ne0\\), then\n\\(\\text{ass:multinomial-base-convergence}\\) and\n\\(\\text{ass:multinomial-local-expansion}\\) give\n\\[\n \\sup_{u\\in C}\\|p_n(u)-p_0\\|_2\n \\leq \\|p_n(0)-p_0\\|_2\n +n^{-1/2}\\sup_{u\\in C}\\|Bu\\|_2+o(n^{-1/2})\n \\longrightarrow0.\n\\tag{8}\n\\]\nThus every nonzero base sign is also eventually its frozen sign,\nuniformly on \\(C\\).  A zero-base cut with zero tangent normal is, by\n\\(\\text{def:label-fan}\\), a fixed tie included in all of its incident\ncompletions.  The complete finite cut list therefore has exactly the\nsame branch signs for the multinomial rule and the offset arrangement\non \\(C\\).  By \\(\\text{def:multinomial-label-regions}\\),\n\\[\n \\mathcal V_n(u)=\\{v:u\\in D_v^0(c)\\}\n \\qquad\\text{for every \\(u\\in C\\)}\n\\tag{9}\n\\]\nfor all sufficiently large \\(n\\).  The compact-domain lemma ensures\nsimultaneously that \\(C\\subseteq\\mathcal U_n\\), so every label on the\nleft side of (9) is lawful.\n\nFinally suppose that\n\\(\\mathcal J_0^{\\mathrm{act}}=\\varnothing\\).  Every retained tangent\ncell is then all of \\(\\mathbb R^d\\).  The equivalence step in the\ndefinition of the semantic map identifies patterns with the same\ncompleted tangent region and retains only one representative, so there\nis one global semantic label, say \\(v_0\\).  The deterministic rule\nreporting \\(\\{v_0\\}\\) has coverage one at every mean and\n\\(\\ell(\\{v_0\\})=\\delta(v_0,v_0)=0\\).  Since diameter loss is\nnonnegative, its honest minimax value is therefore zero.",
